6,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":66.7,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.07332582020264589,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":10.7,"_gate_rev_durability":0.02340124004651356,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":36.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.07284617971091316,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":92.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.03915691631992324,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":98.9,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008286630176417994,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":86.2,"_gate_insider_own":0.29132998,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":100.0,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Great Southern Bancorp, Inc. operates as a bank holding company for Great Southern Bank that provides a range of financial services in Missouri, Iowa, Kansas, Minnesota, Nebraska and Arkansas. The company's deposit products include regular savings accounts, checking accounts, money market accounts, fixed interest rate certificates with varying maturities, certificates of deposit, brokered certificates, and individual retirement accounts. Its loan portfolio comprises residential and commercial real estate loans, commercial business loans, construction loans, home improvement loans, and unsecured consumer loans, as well as secured consumer loans, such as automobile loans, boat loans, home equity loans, and loans secured by savings deposits. It also provides insurance and merchant banking services. Great Southern Bancorp, Inc. was founded in 1923 and is headquartered in Springfield, Missouri.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Joseph William Turner J.D. | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2017)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 857 people. Revenue per employee of $268K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers. Each employee generates $82K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Great Southern Bancorp, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $867M market cap on $229M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -1% over the past three years and +2% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 19% against a 8% cost of capital \u2014 a 11-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $70M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 31 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.15\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 7.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 29% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2986087156490745},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.2% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 9% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Shares offer a 29% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","34 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Why (GSBC) Price Action Is Critical for Tactical Trading","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/90/Why_GSBC_Price_Action_Is_Critical_for_Tactical_Trading_111126032401_1794428641.html","date":"2026-11-11","timestamp":1794428641.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.128,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (GSBC) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktraders